Document ID / Reference Number: DHF-HRC-0004, Rev. 2
Document Title: Heracles Software Architecture Description
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High Level System Architecture

Main Modules

The design of the application is based on the MVVM pattern. There are three core components in the MVVM pattern: the model, the view, and the view model. Each serves a distinct purpose. The diagram below shows the relationships between the three components.

The MVVN design pattern is implemented in the application as follows: the 4 th layer is the gRPC wrapper for communication with Record and Verify services.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H10SG-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-11
TITLE: Data management API
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall use a streaming communication (API) to store and retrieve data remotely from/to the centralized data storage (Database) to allow seamless and sustainable integration.

The list of API functions is defined in the following protocol document:

Heracles DB API
<<<

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10SG-12
TITLE: Patients' Data Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall include a centralized and secure data repository for storing and managing all treatment planning data, including patient information, imaging data, treatment plans, and treatment history.

Patient Table will be stored in a secure manner, and data will be encrypted.

The data shall be managed in a relational database, which shall support hierarchical organization based on user flow.

Entity Relationship Diagram

